      diveDeep: 'When reading hill summits on topographic maps, remember that the summit elevation is not precisely known from contour lines alone — it lies within the interval above the highest closed contour. If the highest closed contour is 220 ft and the interval is 20 ft, the summit is between 220 and 240 ft. You cannot say it is exactly 220 ft or 240 ft. This type of "between which two values" question is very common on the Regents. Contour interval, the difference in elevation between adjacent lines, must always be identified first.',
